{"name":"Banana Peel","hex":"#ffe774","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banana peel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The several outermost layers of a banana, especially once removed from the rest of the banana, which may be slippery if stepped on.","A cause of difficulty, or potential embarrassment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana_peel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Banana Peel","blocks":[{"text":"Banana Peel is a 1963 French-Italian-German comedy film starring Jeanne Moreau and Jean Paul Belmondo. The costumes were created by Pierre Cardin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Banana_Peel_fr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_Peel","wikidata":"Q3373881"},{"title":"Banana peel","blocks":[{"text":"A banana peel, called banana skin in British English, is the outer covering of a banana. Banana peels are used as food for animals, an ingredient in cooking, in water purification, for manufacturing of several biochemical products as well as for jokes and comical situations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg/330px-Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_peel","wikidata":"Q13411117"},{"title":"Peel (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"Peel, also known as rind or skin, is the outer protective layer of a fruit or vegetable which can be peeled off. The rind is usually the botanical exocarp, but the term exocarp also includes the hard cases of nuts, which are not named peels since they are not peeled off by hand or peeler, but rather shells because of their hardness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Orange_zest_and_peel.jpg/330px-Orange_zest_and_peel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peel_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q171187"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg/500px-Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg/1280px-Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg/500px-Banane-A-05_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Discarded banana peels","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanane-A-05_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Banana_peel_on_the_ground.jpg/500px-Banana_peel_on_the_ground.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Banana_peel_on_the_ground.jpg/1280p